      <div class="ltasc-line ltasc-muted">&nbsp;</div>
      <div class="ltasc-line ltasc-muted">...</div>
    </div>
    <div class="ltasc-doc-footer">Reconstruction based on multiple source descriptions. The exact surrounding text is inferred; the command string is confirmed. Clerk has since removed it.</div>
  </div>

  <p>The command string is confirmed by multiple sources and corroborated by the existence of the malicious package at that exact name. Clerk had not published <code>clerk-next-fix-auth-protection</code> as a standalone npm package. The intended binary was bundled inside the scoped package <code>@clerk/eslint-plugin</code>. The bare name sat unclaimed on the public registry.</p>
  <p>Until someone claimed it.</p>
